  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive). Pattern: Xを{弾|はじ}く.\n\nHOMOGRAPH NOTE:\nDo not confuse with {弾|ひ}く (to play a stringed instrument), which uses the same kanji but a different reading.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {指|ゆび}で{弾|はじ}く: to flick with a finger\n- {水|みず}を{弾|はじ}く: to repel water\n- そろばんを{弾|はじ}く: to use an abacus; to calculate\n- {原価|げんか}を{弾|はじ}く: to work out the cost\n\nUSAGE:\nSense 3 originates from the physical act of operating abacus beads. In modern usage, そろばんを{弾|はじ}く can also mean \"to calculate profit/loss\" with a connotation of shrewdness.",
